body:
Greg's words (2026-11-07, via Kimi::Consultant #95 and Fable2 #4823), verbatim: „Wszystko, czego nie ma w uzgodnionej definicji credit, nie może blokować credit. Może zostać zapisane jako diagnostyka.” With #759: „Zadnych nowych warunków”.

Every review brief for Unified EO candidates must carry BOTH quotes verbatim. Reviewers judge correctness only against the agreed credit definition:
- the declared command is the first tool action;
- the host observes the result, and the artifact is the verdict;
- the full source_id at S0 equals the one after, with a dirty tree allowed;
- the existing identity, claim, root, store and committed-declaration checks;
- the w-24a7 C3 start and chronology checks.

Anything else may at most be recorded as a diagnostic, never as a refusal. A finding that asks for one is out of scope and is not a Medium.
